<title>FRANCE: Arthuis urges informal euro-zone stability council.</title>
<headline>Arthuis urges informal euro-zone stability council.</headline>
<dateline>LYON, France 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Finance Minister Jean Arthuis said on Wednesday that France was fully committed to the independence of the European Central Bank which will be set up under European monetary union.</p>
<p>He also repeated that that he wanted a stability council to be set up to coordinate economic, fiscal and currency policy inside the euro zone. This would be an informal council among those inside monetary union and would not in any way impinge on the central bank's independence.</p>
<p>He was speaking at a news conference after talks with German Finance Minister Theo Waigel and French and German central bank heads Jean-Claude Trichet and Hans Tietmeyer.</p>
</text>
